       "reasons": [
        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/dq126tp4234.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "Pencil, treble edge. Six figures grouped 2 + 2 + 2, all of them cut along the top by the crop edge, which begins at the first row of ink. The last two are the same figure, a hooked top with a diagonal and a base, giving the year 22; the middle pair are a plain diagonal and an oval, giving the month 10; the first is a 2. The second figure shows two lobes and looks like the open-topped 8, which would make the day 28, but it is not legible enough to fix and I have not completed it. Crops 2 to 4 carry only a repair patch and stains."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
